LegalEase – Project Documentation Phase
1. Purpose
The documentation phase records all information about the LegalEase project, including its requirements, design, development, testing, and implementation.
2. Documents Prepared
Project Overview: Introduction, objectives, and scope.
Requirement Document: Functional and non-functional requirements.
Design Document: System architecture, modules, database, and UI design.
Development Documentation: Technologies, code structure, and implementation details.
Testing Document: Test cases, results, and bug fixes.
User Manual: Instructions for using the LegalEase website.
Installation Guide: Steps required to install and run the application.
Maintenance Document: Information about future updates and improvements.
3. User Manual
The manual explains how users can:
Register or log in.
Select a legal document type.
Enter the required information.
Generate a document draft.
Review and edit the draft.
Save or download the document.
4. Technical Documentation
It includes:
System architecture
Database structure
API details
AI integration
Software and hardware requirements
Security measures
5. Final Project Report
The final report contains the complete project journey:
Planning → Requirements → Design → Development → Testing → Documentation → Deployment
6. Expected Outcome
Proper documentation makes the LegalEase project easier to understand, maintain, test, modify, and develop further.
